			</heading>
			<begin-paragraph>
			</begin-paragraph>
			<v n="1">he<crossref let="y" cid="c20021001.1" />turns it wherever he will .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021002">
			</marker>
			<v n="2">but the Lord<crossref let="a" cid="c20021002.1" />weighs the heart .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021003">
			</marker>
			<v n="3">is more acceptable to the Lord than sacrifice .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021004">
			</marker>
			<v n="4">
				<crossref let="d" cid="c20021004.2" />the lamp of the wicked , are sin .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021005">
			</marker>
			<v n="5">but everyone who is<crossref let="f" cid="c20021005.2" />hasty comes<crossref let="g" cid="c20021005.3" />only to poverty .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021006">
			</marker>
			<v n="6">is a<crossref let="i" cid="c20021006.2" />fleeting<crossref let="j" cid="c20021006.3" />vapor and a<crossref let="k" cid="c20021006.4" />snare of death .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021007">
			</marker>
			<v n="7">because they refuse to do what is just .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021008">
			</marker>
			<v n="8">but the conduct of the pure is upright .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021009">
			</marker>
			<v n="9">than in a house shared with a quarrelsome wife .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021010">
			</marker>
			<v n="10">his neighbor finds no mercy in his eyes .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021011">
			</marker>
			<v n="11">when a wise man is instructed , he gains knowledge .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021012">
			</marker>
			<v n="12">he throws the wicked down to ruin .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021013">
			</marker>
			<v n="13">will himself call out and not be answered .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021014">
			</marker>
			<v n="14">and a concealed bribe , strong wrath .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021015">
			</marker>
			<v n="15">
				<crossref let="s" cid="c20021015.1" />but terror to evildoers .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021016">
			</marker>
			<v n="16">
				<crossref let="t" cid="c20021016.1" />will rest in the assembly of the dead .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021017">
			</marker>
			<v n="17">he who loves wine and oil will not be rich .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021018">
			</marker>
			<v n="18">and the traitor for the upright .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021019">
			</marker>
			<v n="19">than with a quarrelsome and fretful woman .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021020">
			</marker>
			<v n="20">but a foolish man<crossref let="y" cid="c20021020.2" />devours it .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021021">
			</marker>
			<v n="21">will find<crossref let="a" cid="c20021021.1" />life , righteousness , and honor .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021022">
			</marker>
			<v n="22">and brings down the stronghold in which they trust .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021023">
			</marker>
			<v n="23">
				<crossref let="d" cid="c20021023.2" />keeps himself out of<crossref let="e" cid="c20021023.3" />trouble .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021024">
			</marker>
			<v n="24">who acts with arrogant pride .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021025">
			</marker>
			<v n="25">for his hands refuse to labor .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021026">
			</marker>
			<v n="26">but the righteous<crossref let="h" cid="c20021026.1" />gives and does not hold back .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021027">
			</marker>
			<v n="27">how much more<crossref let="j" cid="c20021027.2" />when he brings it with evil intent .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021028">
			</marker>
			<v n="28">but the word of a man who hears will endure .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021029">
			</marker>
			<v n="29">but the upright<crossref let="l" cid="c20021029.1" />gives thought to his ways .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021030">
			</marker>
			<v n="30">can avail against the Lord .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021031">
			</marker>
			<v n="31">but<crossref let="o" cid="c20021031.2" />the victory belongs to the Lord .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20021032">
			</marker>
